      "claim": "The phrase “two principal answers” to whether life has meaning refers to the main philosophical dichotomy about the source of meaning (objective vs. subjective).",
      "evidence": "Standard philosophy of religion and existentialism textbooks (e.g., Nagel & Miller’s *The Meaning of Life: A Reader*, Wolf’s “Meaning in Life and Why It Matters”) present the debate as a split between an external/objective source of meaning and an internal/subjective source.",
